   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Vaginal discharge: physiologic, or which of four? pH → whiff → wet mount decide",
   "lines": [
    "1 · HISTORY: amount, colour, ODOUR, itch, sexual + Pap history → 2 · SPECULUM: swab the LATERAL walls, not the cervix (blood pH 7)",
    "3 · pH strip, read WET → 4 · WHIFF: 10% KOH, fishy = amines → 5 · WET MOUNT: saline + KOH, low + high power",
    "physiologic: estrogen drives it (lots in pregnancy) · lactobacilli keep it acidic · colour charts are a guide only"
   ]
  },
